Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 3, patch 10 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M14;
 Review 80, the SM seat's finding 12, checked by main): B1893'S LOCK, ITS PAGE
 AND REGISTER ROW P-816 SAY WHICH HALF OF THE TEST WOULD TELL MAIN.

The lock asserts that a ceiling which falls and rises back is still not seen, for two ceilings, and its docstring said that the first assertion of each pair fails when the gap is closed. That holds for the first pair, which plants a history of the identification baseline in a small repository and asks the gate. It does not hold for the second: for the attribution ceiling the first assertion gives the two-point rule the same count at both ends, with no history, and a mend that reads the ceiling along its history leaves it true.

A dated note says so in the docstring, under the page's paragraph, and in row P-816. No assertion is changed. The lock: 7 tests pass.

SAID BY THE SESSION THAT BUILDS THE MEND: the series that reads both ceilings along their history is built and not sent (series 5 of the enforcement package, its eighth patch). On it this test's first assertion fails, as the docstring says it will, and the second pair's does not. 0 of 19.
